course: dictionary
lesson: 2378
title: Cupcake: a small cake in a cup
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cupcake is a small cake baked in a paper or foil cup, often with icing on top. You may not need a dictionary for this word, because the sentence around it gives clues. «On her last day Maddie gives everyone a cupcake.» Maddie hands one to every person, so a cupcake is something small you can share and eat.
explain: Look for clues about where cupcakes come from. «And when Amara brings shop biscuits to the cake sale because Mum had no time or eggs, they help just as much as homemade cupcakes.» Homemade means made at home, so cupcakes can be baked by a family, and they are often sold at a cake sale.
explain: Try the swap test. Put "small cake" in place of cupcake: "On her last day Maddie gives everyone a small cake." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A cupcake is a small cake baked in a paper or foil cup, often with icing on top.
fact: A dozen cupcakes is 12 cupcakes.
fact: In maths, a tray of cupcakes is a total: trays × cupcakes on each tray gives the total, and total ÷ people gives how many each person gets.
fact: Cupcakes often appear at school bake sales and birthday treats.
fact: Before you bake or share cupcakes, wash your hands, use oven gloves, and check for allergies.
exercise: «On her last day Maddie gives everyone a cupcake.» What is a cupcake? | A type of biscuit that is never iced | *A small cake baked in a paper or foil cup | A cup of hot chocolate | A large loaf of bread
exercise: A baker fills 4 trays with 6 cupcakes on each tray. How many cupcakes is that? | 46 | *24 | 10 | 12
exercise: Mum bakes 36 cupcakes and shares them equally between 9 children. How many does each child get? | 3 | *4 | 27 | 45
test: Before you share cupcakes at school, what should you do first? | Lick the icing off the bowl | *Wash your hands and check for allergies | Eat one to check it | Put them in a bag with no label
test: A dozen cupcakes is how many cupcakes? | 24 | 10 | 1 | *12
exam: Mia has 3 boxes with 8 cupcakes in each box and shares them equally between 4 friends. How many cupcakes does each friend get? | 12 | *6 | 32 | 2
